===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=pillar|:inh|enm:post<ety:inh<ang:post>:bor<fro:post<ety:der<la:postis>>>>|tree=1}}
{{inh+|en|enm|post}}, from {{der|en|ang|post||pillar, door-post}} and {{der|en|fro|post||post, upright beam}}, both from {{der|en|la|postis||door, post, doorpost}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A long [[dowel]] or [[plank]] protruding from the ground; a [[fencepost]]; a [[lightpost]].
#: {{ux|en|ram a '''post''' into the ground}}
## A [[pole]] erected to mark a spot.
##: {{ux|en|The '''posts''' mark the boundaries of the property.}}
## {{lb|en|horse-racing}} The stakes that mark the beginning or end of a [[horse race]]
## {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[doorpost]] of a [[victualler]]'s shop or inn, on which were chalked the [[score]]s of [[customer]]s; hence, a score; a [[debt]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1600|author=w:Samuel Rowlands|title=The knauve of clubs
|passage=when God ſends coyne, <br>I will diſcharge your '''poaſt'''}}
## {{lb|en|sports}} A [[goalpost]].
##* {{quote-web|en|date=December 29, 2010| author=Chris Whyatt| title=Chelsea 1 - 0 Bolton| work=BBC| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9309542.stm| passage=But they marginally improved after the break as {{w|Didier Drogba}} hit the '''post'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260204040745/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9309542.stm|archivedate=4 February 2026}}
## {{lb|en|dentistry}} A long, narrow piece inserted into a [[root canal]] to provide retention for a crown.
## {{lb|en|construction}} A [[stud]]; a [[two-by-four]].
## {{lb|en|jewelry}} The wire-like core of metal in an [[earring]].
# A [[pole]] in a [[battery]].
# {{lb|en|vocal|_|music|chiefly|a cappella}} A prolonged final [[melody]] note, among moving [[harmony]] notes.
# {{lb|en|paper|printing}} A [[printing]] [[paper]] size measuring 19.25 inches x 15.5 inches.
# {{lb|en|crochet}} The vertical part of a [[crochet]] stitch.

